=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_e7a3 — Standard split-shift revised; guitar on couch weekend evenings, blanket on bed weekend mornings (fork of p_a3f7)

This is a revision of the top-weight standard split-shift document. Two changes are forced by the latest sightings. First, the guitar: on the Saturday 21:00 patrol the robot found guitar_hana on couch_l1 twice (and once still on bedroom_floor_b1 in the same pass), which directly contradicts the parent's "guitar never leaves bedroom_floor_b1" claim. Hana is home all weekend and evidently drags her guitar out to the couch for an evening playing session. I add a weekend-evening block (20:00–23:00) at couch_l1 with chance "sometimes" (she does not do this every single weekend evening, but the pattern is now established). Second, the blanket: on Saturday 03:00, 07:00, and 08:00 the robot found blanket_shared on bed_b1, not on the coffee table or couch. On weekends, when both residents sleep in later and the house is quieter, the blanket is pulled up onto the bed as a sleep blanket. I add a weekend-morning block (0:00–09:00) at bed_b1. I also correct the weekday base for the blanket from coffee_table_l1 to couch_l1, because the weekday sightings (16:00, 17:00, 19:00) overwhelmingly show the couch, with only occasional coffee_table passes.

Everything else in the parent document is retained: Priya's walks and errands, Hana's 13:40–23:00 shift, the camera on the bookshelf, the yoga mat in wardrobe_b2, the meal and TV schedules.

What sets this apart from the parent: guitar_hana at couch_l1 on weekend evenings; blanket_shared at bed_b1 on weekend mornings; blanket base is couch_l1 (not coffee_table_l1) on weekdays. What would refute it: guitar_hana sighted at couch_l1 on a weekday (she is at work); blanket_shared sighted at coffee_table_l1 on a weekend morning.

